title the return nobody read; three silences under one witness, and %282 closes
prompt Keaton opened Sound on the macOS bench -- read Kyri and Gauge, honor the INNER LOOP, take the widened constellation lane core-first, hold the Pond accrete-only boundary, send the twice-pulled way, stop at the custody gates.
think The cold roster ran alone this time -- no peer session, pgrep read only my own -- and closed honest: 71 guards, 69 green, 2 red, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close. That matters because last lap two of three roster reds were manufactured by a second session writing this checkout, and the guard that would tell the difference is tree_moved. It read no, so both reds are the tree's own.
think caravan_suite red at caravan_harvest_witness, the rung last lap proved GREEN. Rather than argue I measured: 3 runs idle GREEN, 1 under load GREEN, 1 from a cold caravan/bin GREEN, then 6 more at load average 76 all GREEN -- eleven for eleven. The sub-readings held too: the load-bearing line the witness asserts exactly, idle beside a ready slot ... by readiness 0, stood 12 of 12 under load. What DOES move under load is the raw idle count one line above, which reads by readiness 0, 1 or 2 and is always 0 idle -- and the witness comment says that count is read without being asserted while the line below asserts a prefix of it. Comment and code disagree there, which is worth a lap of its own. I could not reproduce the red and I am not going to invent a cause for it.
think %282's last leg was mine and definite. mantra/recall_subscribe_poll_delivery.rye declared SOL_SOCKET 1, SO_REUSEADDR 2, SO_RCVTIMEO 20. A C probe compiled against this bench's own headers answered 65535, 4, 4102, and setsockopt(level=1, opt=2) returned rc=-1 errno=22 EINVAL. Worth saying exactly: those are not the Linux column, they are the x86-64 Linux column -- rye/lib/std/os/linux.zig dispatches SO on architecture and answers 65535/4/4102 on mips and 1/4/8192 on sparc, inside a module this tree cross-builds for riscv64.
think The reason three wrong numbers survived the module's whole life is one character: both call sites read `_ = c.setsockopt(...)`. The refusal came back every time and was thrown away. With the receive timeout never reaching a socket, recvfrom blocks forever -- so three source-loop children orphaned by earlier runs were still alive 67 minutes later, one holding UDP 127.0.0.1:38487, and that held port is what refused the next run's bind. BindFailed was the fourth consequence of a discarded return, not a fault of its own.
think Fixing the module moved the red rather than closing it: bind worked, and the signal witness still failed with the service never GREEN. The last fault was the witness. It ran `rm -f ... && ${service} ... &`, and & backgrounds the whole compound, so $! named the subshell. Measured directly: $! was 40851 and the supervisor was 40854, and kill -TERM terminated 40851 while 40854 ran on unsignalled. exec makes the subshell become the service -- one pid, 40926, signal lands, graceful stop, no orphan. This is the card's own killing a rishi wrapper orphans its sh child, firing a second time in another room.
obs Council rota N=3525 mod 5 = 0 -- Aether, the row that hears, which is this star's own row and its fixed seat. It read as instruction rather than decoration: the fixed pair is sound and silence, and this whole lap was about a silence. A guard that cannot red guards nothing is the grain strand the Aether dual seat names, and a setsockopt whose return is discarded is exactly that -- a check with no voice. flock was absent and said so; the waitpid 9 answered plausibly; this one never spoke at all, and the third is the quietest and the most expensive.
obs The REDS pin hit the wall last lap forecast. At 24,573 of 24,576 there were three bytes, and an honest closure needs about seven hundred. reds_fold.sh refuses %273 because its text reads OPEN none and the test matches the bare word -- correct conservatism for a tool that moves rows, and the phrasing belongs to a dated row, so I left the guard alone and named both. What worked instead: close %282 briefly so it folds, then give the full account on its shelf, where no byte bound applies. Pin 24,573 to 23,153, spine 1..282 with no gaps, headline regenerated by its own writer.
obs Sweep before fix, since a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom. The subshell shape is unique -- three other dollar-bang sites background a simple command, so $! names it correctly. The constant shape is not: 19 files still declare SOL_SOCKET: c_int = 1 and 25 setsockopt returns across 19 files are still discarded. That is a lap per module with its own witness run, so it is a card line rather than this lap's tail.
obs The Pond accrete-only boundary was not approached -- no ai-jail markdown touched. The adaptation grant went unspent; no bash, HTML or Python stood in this red's way. The seed cadence stays Dream's and publish-seed.sh was not run.
loom probe kernel_sol=65535 kernel_reuseaddr=4 kernel_rcvtimeo=4102 rye_spelled=1,2,20 setsockopt_rc=-1 errno=22
loom orphans count=3 lifetime_min=67 port_held=38487 after_fix=0
loom signal dollar_bang_pid=40851 service_pid=40854 with_exec_pid=40926 orphans_after=0
loom subscribe_poll witnesses_green=4of4 was=3of4
loom harvest direct_runs=11 green=11 red_in_suite=1 load_avg_max=76
loom stagger asserted_line_held=12of12 raw_readiness_idle=0,1,2 idle_always=0
loom roster guards_run=71 green=69 red=2 tree_moved=no
loom sweep files_linux_column=19 discarded_setsockopt=25 files_with_discards=19
loom reds pin_before=24573 pin_after=23153 bound=24576 spine=282
file mantra/recall_subscribe_poll_delivery.rye five socket constants reach std.c; both setsockopt returns checked with named errors
file tools/ca/caravan_subscribe_poll_signal.rish exec so the backgrounded subshell becomes the service and dollar-bang names it
file construction/REDS.md %282 closed and folded; the pin keeps what is open
