recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two things want your word. %281 is unchanged and still yours: this lap ran alone and the roster proved it with tree_moved=no, which is the argument for one tree per star. And the REDS pin is at its wall -- a closure now costs a fold every time, and reds_fold.sh cannot fold %273 while its dated text reads OPEN none, so the pin's one closed row is stuck. Ungated and ready as the next kg: the 19-file socket-constant sweep, one module per lap with its own witness; and the caravan_harvest comment that says a count is read without being asserted while the line below asserts it.
